.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1203:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:377:640:- L3 wave adversarial: codex-challenge + architect-reviewer + **full Suite S re-run** (DOS-287 cross-entity bleed reproduction blocked; no PII in fixtures; secrets handling end-to-end; compliance-auditor pass) + **full Suite P re-run** (burst signal storms, coalescing bounds, release-gate latency budget) + **Suite E final** (bundles 1+5 mandatory pass; bundles 2-4, 6-8 reports filed as v1.4.1 follow-ups if failing)
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1205:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:394:    13	Scope limits stay strict. DOS-259 does not implement production prompt fingerprinting; DOS-213 consumes this hook later. It does not add OpenAI/Ollama providers. It does not ship the W4-B/DOS-216 evaluation fixture format. It does not change claims, provenance storage, or derived-state writes.
