.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:1833:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-5.log:9681:+The new risk is scoring a wrong-subject claim as reliable because its source is reliable. W3-B's `SubjectAttribution` fails ambiguous/blocked subject fit for claim-bearing output (`.docs/plans/wave-W3/DOS-211-plan.md:57-59`), ADR-0123 `WrongSubject` creates per-subject tombstone behavior (`.docs/decisions/0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md:45-54`, `:129-142`), and W4-A additionally downranks `subject_fit_confidence` / `cross_entity_coherence`.
