.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2117:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1470:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:158:**`effective` is computed by the provenance builder, not the author.** The author cannot set it; the registry rejects manually-constructed `Provenance` with mismatched `effective` and `contributions`.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2118:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1471:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:165:pub struct SourceAttribution {
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2119:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1472:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:169:    pub source_asof: Option<DateTime<Utc>>,      // When the source itself was authored (if known)
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2120:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1473:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:237:1. Every field in the ability's domain output MUST have an entry in `field_attributions`. No "optional for Read" escape hatch — Read abilities' fields are typically `Direct` with `ConfidenceKind::Implicit`, which is trivial to populate but must exist.
