.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2125:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1481:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:277:    let mut prov = ProvenanceBuilder::new(ctx, "prepare_meeting");
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2126:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1483:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:310:- Wraps the domain output in `AbilityOutput<T>` with the built provenance.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2127:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1484:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:315:Provenance persists anywhere the ability output is stored. Specifically:
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2128:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1485:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:317:1. **Maintenance audit table.** [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §8 `MaintenanceAuditRecord` adds a `provenance: Provenance` field. Source revocation triggers a masking pass: a `Provenance` whose sources reference a revoked `DataSource` is replaced with a `ProvenanceMasked` marker per [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md). **Interaction with [ADR-0094](0094-audit-log-and-enterprise-observability.md):** ADR-0094's append-only JSONL security audit remains unchanged. The `maintenance_audit` SQLite table is a separate operational log for runtime diagnostics. Provenance content in the operational log is subject to masking; the JSONL security log is unchanged.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2129:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1486:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:319:2. **Outbox table.** [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §2 outbox entries add a `provenance: Provenance` field. Outbox provenance captures the ability's full output-time provenance, including the invocation that generated the pending external mutation.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2130:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1487:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:325:**Storage format.** Provenance is stored as JSON in a single column per containing record. Indexes on `invocation_id`, `ability_name`, `produced_at`, and `data_source` (via a normalized xref table) support the queries [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §8 requires. A full JSON-column approach is feasible at the six-user scale; if scale changes, a normalized `provenance` / `provenance_sources` split can be introduced without changing the envelope contract.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2131:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1488:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:333:**Hard truncation.** When a provenance envelope exceeds 1MB at finalize time, composition subtrees are collapsed from deepest first into a `ProvenanceWarning::DepthElided` summary carrying aggregate source counts and trust classification. Truncation is a finalize-time concern; the full tree never leaves the ability in its raw form above the hard limit.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2132:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1489:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:341:3. **Scoped reproducibility.** The `InputsSnapshot` supports staleness detection, diff reasoning, and fixture-mode replay — the three use cases that actually matter — without overpromising exact content-level replay of live runs.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2133:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1490:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:343:5. **Source revocation can cascade correctly.** Provenance references `DataSource` via [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md), and lifecycle behavior (purge vs. flag) is governed by that ADR. Masking shape is governed by [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md).
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2134:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1491:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:348:1. **Every ability pays an authoring cost.** Provenance building is part of the ability's job. Contributors must think about source attribution when writing synthesis.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2135:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1492:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:349:2. **Provenance can be large.** Deep composition with full field attribution produces substantial JSON. Soft budget warns; hard truncation bounds worst-case.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2136:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1493:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:357:3. **Storage volume growth.** Provenance retained indefinitely alongside outputs accumulates. Mitigation: same retention as output; no separate provenance retention policy.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2137:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1495:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:364:- [ADR-0102: Abilities as the Runtime Contract](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) — Defines `AbilityOutput<T>` wrapper; §9 Rule 5 requires provenance; §10 consumes `TrustAssessment`; §11.3 requires composition merge.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2138:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1496:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:365:- [ADR-0103: Maintenance Ability Safety Constraints](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) — §8 maintenance audit records add a `provenance: Provenance` field per §8 of this ADR.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2139:.docs/plans/wave-W4/_prompts/_logs/DOS-216.log:1497:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:371:- **[ADR-0108: Provenance Rendering and Privacy](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md)** — Per-surface rendering rules, actor-filtered display, `ProvenanceMasked` shape, sanitization of `explanation` text, and P2 publication safety.
