.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2841:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:30:- Each feedback type maps to a distinct trust/provenance operation per ticket §"Trust/Provenance Semantics".
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2849:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:262:566:- L3 wave adversarial: codex-challenge + architect-reviewer + **Suite S report** (auth/authz on `invoke_ability`, MCP actor-filter discovery, schema-validation on input JSON, capability-handle leakage) + **Suite P report** (trust math at claim-volume — within p99 < 5ms provisional) + **Suite E report** (cross-entity-coherence factor lights up on bundle-1 fixture; bundle-5 correction-resurrection green)
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2850:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:265:640:- L3 wave adversarial: codex-challenge + architect-reviewer + **full Suite S re-run** (DOS-287 cross-entity bleed reproduction blocked; no PII in fixtures; secrets handling end-to-end; compliance-auditor pass) + **full Suite P re-run** (burst signal storms, coalescing bounds, release-gate latency budget) + **Suite E final** (bundles 1+5 mandatory pass; bundles 2-4, 6-8 reports filed as v1.4.1 follow-ups if failing)
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2851:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:274:**Extends:** [ADR-0113](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md), [ADR-0114](0114-scoring-unification.md), [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) (SubjectAttribution amendment)
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2854:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:365:    pub subject: SubjectRef,                  // From ADR-0105 SubjectAttribution amendment
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2856:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:419:- `corrected_to: Some(SubjectRef)` — "this content belongs to that entity instead." Tombstone at the asserted subject; propose (not commit) a new claim at the corrected subject with the same claim_text, full provenance preserved, `actor = 'user_correction'`. The corrected claim enters via the standard propose/commit path so it gets the same gate as any other claim.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2860:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:467:- [ADR-0105: Provenance as First-Class Output](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) — `SubjectAttribution` amendment supplies `SubjectRef` consumed by `WrongSubject`.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2862:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:487:Scope limits stay strict. DOS-259 does not implement production prompt fingerprinting; DOS-213 consumes this hook later. It does not add OpenAI/Ollama providers. It does not ship the W4-B/DOS-216 evaluation fixture format. It does not change claims, provenance storage, or derived-state writes.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2871:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:587:The concurrency test drives N simultaneous `.complete()` calls against a fixture-backed provider and proves the `Send + Sync` invariant from ADR-0091. The W2 merge-gate artifact remains `cargo clippy -- -D warnings && cargo test` plus the broader wave gate `pnpm tsc --noEmit`. Suite E contribution is replay-provider coverage on the stub/in-memory fixture. No Suite S or Suite P contribution is expected from this PR beyond the standard gate.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2875:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:874:- **Files owned:** `src-tauri/src/abilities/provenance/` (envelope, builder, TrustAssessment, SourceAttribution, FieldAttribution, SubjectAttribution).
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2887:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:1068:Schema in the migration: `intelligence_claims` with immutable assertion columns (`id`, `subject_ref`, `claim_type`, `field_path` or `topic_key`, `text`, `dedup_key`, `item_hash`, `actor`, `data_source`, `source_ref`, `source_asof`, `observed_at`, `created_at`, `provenance_json`, `metadata_json`), lifecycle columns (`claim_state`, `surfacing_state`, `demotion_reason`, `reactivated_at`, `retraction_reason`, `expires_at`, `superseded_by`, `trust_score`, `trust_computed_at`, `trust_version`, `thread_id`, `temporal_scope`, `sensitivity`), and indexes for default reads plus suppression lookup. Include `thread_id` from ADR-0124 (`.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:33-48`), `source_asof` from ADR-0105 (`.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:391-466`), and `temporal_scope` / `sensitivita defaults.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2971:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:4117:+W3-B supplies `SubjectRef` / provenance source references. `WrongSubject` and `WrongSource` validation must consume those types, not parse ad hoc JSON. W3-G supplies `source_asof`; W3-H supplies claim type registry rules for `NeedsNuance` eligibility. W4 / DOS-5 consumes `claim_feedback`, `agent_trust_ledger`, and trust columns but W3-E owns the per-action semantic map that DOS-5 implements.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-218.log:2972:.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-294.log:4141:+Wave merge-gate contribution: W3-E supplies the feedback-action matrix artifact, render-policy stub evidence, and Suite S checks for enum injection/cross-subject corrections/PII-free activity payloads. Suite P contribution is transaction/query count for feedback writes and repair enqueue caps. Suite E contribution is one fixture per primary action, including hundreds of low/medium claims where only high-impact ambiguous claims enter `needs_user_decision`.
