.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-296.log:9306:+DOS-296 is a substrate-only allowance for longitudinal topic threading. It adds a nullable thread reference to claim storage and an additive `thread_ids` list to Provenance, but does not define what a thread means or how claims enter one. Load-bearing ticket lines: "Add nullable `thread_id TEXT NULL` column to `intelligence_claims` table." "`Provenance.provenance_schema_version` stays at `1` - additive, optional, default-empty field per ADR-0105 §1 forward-compatibility rules." "`dedup_key` formula does NOT include `thread_id` - same-content claims that participate in different threads remain the same claim." "No retrieval logic. No UI. No thread creation. No assignment heuristic."
