.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1270:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:34:- Returns a typed output wrapped in `AbilityOutput<T>`, which carries the domain output alongside a mandatory provenance envelope. Provenance shape is specified in [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md). The domain output itself does not re-embed provenance.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1272:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:53:├── provenance.rs               # Provenance types (detail in ADR-0105)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1273:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:74:Each ability is a single module — typically one file, but a directory is permitted for abilities large enough to warrant submodules (e.g., `prepare_meeting/` containing `mod.rs`, `prompts.rs`, `synthesis.rs`, `tests.rs`). The module has one public entry point (the ability function) and opaque internals. Eval fixtures live under `src-tauri/tests/abilities/{ability_name}/` (detail in [ADR-0107](0107-evaluation-harness-for-abilities.md)).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1285:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:168:    pub provenance: Provenance,           // Canonical location — see ADR-0105
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1286:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:176:- Provenance lives on `AbilityOutput<T>`, exactly one place. Domain output types never re-declare a `provenance` field. Reviewers reject such declarations at registration.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1287:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:177:- Field-level provenance attribution (how `suggested_outcomes[0]` ties back to specific signals) is specified in [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md). This ADR requires that the mechanism exist; 0105 defines the shape.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1295:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:299:Provenance lives exactly once, on the wrapper. Domain output types never re-declare it. The mechanism is what makes depth explainable and quality measurable. Shape specified in [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1297:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:321:- Transform outputs carry a `trust: Trust::Untrusted` marker in their provenance ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md)).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1302:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:353:When ability A invokes ability B, A's provenance envelope includes B's provenance as a nested child. The full provenance tree shows the composition. Deduplication rules and merge semantics specified in [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1308:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:387:`prepare_meeting`, `get_daily_readiness`, `get_entity_context`, `list_open_loops`, `detect_risk_shift` migrate behind abilities. App Tauri commands become thin wrappers. MCP sidecar query handlers become thin wrappers over the same abilities. Parallel-run validation per [ADR-0109](0109-migration-strategy.md).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1318:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:443:- [ADR-0082: Entity-Generic Prep Pipeline](0082-entity-generic-prep-pipeline.md) — The entity model is the substrate on which abilities operate. `get_entity_context` generalizes the prep pipeline.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1320:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:445:- [ADR-0098: Data Governance — Source-Aware Lifecycle](0098-data-governance-source-aware-lifecycle.md) — Data source tagging flows through into ability provenance.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1325:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:450:- **ADR-0105 (forthcoming): Provenance as First-Class Output** — Specifies the provenance shape, field-level attribution, trust markers, merge semantics, and rendering contract referenced throughout this ADR.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1331:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:468:1. **Hard error** — ability returns `Err(AbilityError::...)`. Caller sees no output. Surface decides user-visible message per [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md). No partial data leaks.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1334:.docs/decisions/0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md:483:The `warnings[]` field on Provenance is the canonical record of "what went soft." Surfaces render it per [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1342:.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:6:**Extends:** [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) (SubjectAttribution amendment), [ADR-0113](0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md) (claims)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1344:.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:16:- Multi-subject claims spanning Account / Project / Person / Meeting ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) SubjectAttribution amendment).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1350:.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:48:- Provenance envelope `provenance_schema_version` stays at `1` — the new field is additive, optional, default-empty (forward-compatible per ADR-0105 §1).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1363:.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:141:- [ADR-0105: Provenance as First-Class Output](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) — `SubjectRef::Multi` is what enables a single claim to span the subjects a thread typically does.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1365:.docs/decisions/0124-longitudinal-topic-threading.md:143:- [ADR-0123: Typed Claim Feedback Semantics](0123-typed-claim-feedback-semantics.md) — `WrongSubject` feedback on a thread-attached claim corrects the subject without affecting thread membership.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1501:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:6:**Extends:** [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md), [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md), [ADR-0104](0104-execution-mode-and-mode-aware-services.md), [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md), [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1504:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:14:1. [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) makes every capability a typed, versioned ability. Many of those are Transform abilities that produce claims. The product will ship with multiple ability authors — `prepare_meeting`, `detect_risk_shift`, `generate_weekly_narrative`, future MCP agents — each asserting claims into the same substrate.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1508:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:28:Every claim in `intelligence_claims` carries an `actor` string with one of the following canonical shapes. The `actor` column is non-nullable. Provenance's `Actor` type ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §1) uses the same shape.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1509:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:39:- The `:<version>` suffix on `agent:` is mandatory and matches `ability_version` from provenance ([ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §8).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1512:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:96:- **Transform abilities** produce `AbilityOutput<ClaimProposal>` — synthesized assertions with full provenance, but no side effect on `intelligence_claims`.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1520:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:201:Provenance ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md)) is extended:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1522:.docs/decisions/0113-human-and-agent-analysis-as-first-class-claim-sources.md:209:[ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md)'s `DataSource` enum is **not** extended with new variants for actors. `DataSource` describes the *origin of information* (Glean downstream, Clay, Gong transcript, user input). `actor` describes *who asserted the claim*. A single agent claim has `actor = 'agent:prepare_meeting:1.3'` and sources `[Glean { downstream: Salesforce }, Glean { downstream: Gong }]`. The two axes are orthogonal and remain so.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1560:.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:6:**Extends:** [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md), [ADR-0104](0104-execution-mode-and-mode-aware-services.md), [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1561:.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:7:**Related:** [ADR-0106](0106-prompt-fingerprinting-and-provider-interface.md), [ADR-0110](0110-evaluation-harness-for-abilities.md), [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md), [ADR-0119](0119-runtime-evaluator-pass-for-transform-abilities.md)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1562:.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:13:Twenty v1.4.0 substrate ADRs land claims, provenance, trust scoring, signal propagation, and the runtime evaluator — all of which produce telemetry in some form. Each ADR defines its own telemetry locally: [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) carries the `Provenance` envelope; [ADR-0106](0106-prompt-fingerprinting-and-provider-interface.md) produces `PromptFingerprint`; [ADR-0110](0110-evaluation-harness-for-abilities.md) generates eval run data; [ADR-0119](0119-runtime-evaluator-pass-for-transform-abilities.md) writes `evaluation_traces`.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1563:.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:15:What does not exist is a **cross-cutting contract** that every ability, every service function, and every background worker emits uniformly. The aggregate effect: when something goes wrong in production, an engineer (or Claude Code session) debugging the issue has to stitch together provenance envelopes, ad-hoc `println!`-style logs, `signal_events` rows, and maybe a `tracing` span here and there — every ADR made its own choice and no contract ties them together.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1567:.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:91:- Provenance envelope ([ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md)) already carries `invocation_id`. This ADR reaffirms it as the stable correlation key.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1571:.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:128:The observability contract honors [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md) masking rules. Specifically:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1573:.docs/decisions/0120-observability-contract.md:135:The distinction: logs carry **the shape of what happened**, not **the content of what happened**. Content lives in the encrypted database with the provenance envelopes and `evaluation_traces`. Debug flows pull content at display time through [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md) renderer, not by reading raw logs.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1615:.docs/decisions/0094-audit-log-and-enterprise-observability.md:143:Note: detail fields contain **counts and categories only** -- no names, emails, subject lines, or content. This satisfies the log PII hygiene rule from ADR-0092.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1628:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:1:# ADR-0108: Provenance Rendering and Privacy
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1629:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:6:**Extends:** [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md), [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md)  
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1630:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:7:**Related:** [ADR-0094](0094-audit-log-and-enterprise-observability.md), [ADR-0093](0093-prompt-injection-hardening.md), [ADR-0111](0111-surface-independent-ability-invocation.md)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1631:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:11:[ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) defines the `Provenance` envelope and requires surfaces to render it. It defers three concerns to this ADR:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1632:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:15:3. **The `ProvenanceMasked` shape** referenced by [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §8 and used when sources are revoked.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1633:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:17:[ADR-0094](0094-audit-log-and-enterprise-observability.md) governs the append-only JSONL security audit with strict PII hygiene. [ADR-0093](0093-prompt-injection-hardening.md) established that LLM outputs can contain adversarial content. This ADR integrates both: provenance must be renderable to users and agents without leaking internal graph structure or PII, and sanitization of LLM-generated `explanation` text must prevent re-injection.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1634:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:27:- A secondary "Details" expansion shows field-level attributions: for each significant output field, the sources that contributed, their `data_source` (using human-readable names via [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md)'s `DataSource::display_name()`), and any `confidence` score.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1635:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:33:- Every tool response includes provenance by default. The `Provenance` envelope serializes as a structured field alongside the domain output.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1636:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:50:- The `maintenance_audit` table stores the full `ProvenanceOrMasked` per invocation.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1637:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:52:- [ADR-0094](0094-audit-log-and-enterprise-observability.md)'s append-only JSONL security audit remains unchanged — it captures security events (auth, permissions, source revocations, etc.) with its existing hygiene rules. Provenance lives in the operational `maintenance_audit` SQLite table, separate from the security audit.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1638:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:56:A universal renderer transforms `Provenance` into an actor-appropriate view:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1639:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:59:pub fn render_provenance_for(prov: &Provenance, actor: Actor, surface: Surface) -> RenderedProvenance { ... }
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1640:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:76:LLM-generated `explanation` text is untrusted per [ADR-0093](0093-prompt-injection-hardening.md). It can contain prompt injection attempts, PII from other sources, or links to attacker-controlled content. Every explanation is passed through a sanitizer before rendering:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1641:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:81:4. **Banned token list.** Explanations containing instruction-like phrases common in prompt injection attempts (e.g., "ignore previous", "you are now", "system:") are filtered: the whole explanation is replaced with `[explanation removed by sanitizer]` and a `ProvenanceWarning::ExplanationFiltered` is added.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1642:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:86:### 4. The `ProvenanceMasked` Shape
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1643:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:88:When a source is revoked and its associated provenance records are masked per [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md) §5:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1644:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:91:pub struct ProvenanceMasked {
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1645:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:108:The `ProvenanceOrMasked` enum in [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §8's `MaintenanceAuditRecord` is either the full envelope or this masked placeholder. Consumers handle both.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1646:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:114:[ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §9 specifies storage size budgets. Rendering has its own:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1647:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:120:When rendering exceeds a budget, the renderer truncates deepest-first (children elided first, sources last) and surfaces a `ProvenanceWarning::TruncatedForRender { surface, budget_bytes, original_bytes }`.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1648:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:124:[ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §7 declared "every surface that displays ability output MUST be capable of rendering provenance." This ADR narrows the "MUST" to outputs where provenance rendering is meaningful:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1649:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:136:- Navigation items showing ability-derived names
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1650:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:148:4. **Masking has explicit shape.** `ProvenanceMasked` is defined; consumers handle `ProvenanceOrMasked` uniformly.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1651:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:169:- [ADR-0105: Provenance as First-Class Output](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) — Defines the envelope; this ADR specifies rendering.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1652:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:170:- [ADR-0107: Source Taxonomy Alignment](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md) — Specifies `DataSource::display_name()` and `ScoringClass`; rendering uses both.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1653:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:171:- [ADR-0094: Audit Log and Enterprise Observability](0094-audit-log-and-enterprise-observability.md) — Security audit remains separate from provenance rendering.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1654:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:172:- [ADR-0093: Prompt Injection Hardening](0093-prompt-injection-hardening.md) — Explanation sanitizer aligns with ADR-0093's untrusted-content rules.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1655:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:173:- [ADR-0103: Maintenance Ability Safety Constraints](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) — `MaintenanceAuditRecord` carries `ProvenanceOrMasked` per this ADR's §4.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1656:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:174:- **ADR-0111 (forthcoming): Surface-Independent Ability Invocation** — Consumes the per-surface rendering rules specified here.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1657:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:186:- The cap applies to the full `Provenance` envelope after JSON serialization, before any surface rendering.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1658:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:187:- Abilities that would exceed the cap return `Err(AbilityError::ProvenanceTooLarge { size_bytes, cap_bytes })`. No silent truncation.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1659:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:188:- The cap is enforced at `AbilityOutput<T>` construction time. The error surfaces to the caller as a hard error (per [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) error-handling amendment).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1660:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:192:1. **Provenance summarization** — collapse deep composition trees into summary nodes marked `ProvenanceWarning::DepthElided`. [ADR-0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) §1 already declares this warning class; this amendment activates it.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1661:.docs/decisions/0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md:194:3. **Conscious cap increase** — via ADR amendment, after measuring real production composition shapes. Not an automatic bump.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1704:.docs/decisions/README.md:124:| [0105](0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md) | Provenance as first-class output (v1.4.0 trust/attribution/reproducibility) | Proposed |
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1705:.docs/decisions/README.md:127:| [0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md) | Provenance rendering, per-surface rules, and privacy (v1.4.0) | Proposed |
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1729:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:1:# ADR-0105: Provenance as First-Class Output
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1730:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:6:**Extends:** [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md)  
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1731:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:7:**Depends on:** [ADR-0104](0104-execution-mode-and-mode-aware-services.md)  
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1732:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:8:**Required by:** [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §8 (audit), [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §10 (trust boundary)  
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1733:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:9:**Companions:** [ADR-0106](0106-prompt-fingerprinting-and-provider-interface.md) (prompt fingerprint details), [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md) (`DataSource` taxonomy), [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md) (surface rendering and safety)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1734:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:13:[ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §9 Rule 5 declares that every ability output carries provenance via `AbilityOutput<T>`. §10 declares Transform outputs are untrusted for mutation authorization. §11.3 declares composition produces nested provenance trees. [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §8 requires maintenance audit records to carry provenance. All of these contracts depend on one shape: the `Provenance` envelope. ADR-0102 references it but does not specify it.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1735:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:15:This ADR defines the envelope shape, trust classification, and composition semantics. It deliberately does not define: prompt fingerprinting (see [ADR-0106](0106-prompt-fingerprinting-and-provider-interface.md)), the authoritative `DataSource` taxonomy (see [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md)), or per-surface rendering rules (see [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md)). Splitting these concerns keeps each ADR implementable atomically and testable in isolation.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1736:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:19:Every ability output carries a `Provenance` envelope via the `AbilityOutput<T>` wrapper from [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §6. The envelope captures identity, temporal context, trust classification, source attribution, composition tree, and field-level attribution.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1737:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:21:### 1. The Provenance Envelope
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1738:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:24:pub struct Provenance {
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1739:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:25:    // Envelope schema version — for forward-compatibility on this ADR's structure itself
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1740:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:31:    pub ability_schema_version: SchemaVersion,   // The ability's I/O schema version, per ADR-0102 §8
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1741:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:35:    pub produced_at: DateTime<Utc>,              // From ctx.services.clock.now() per ADR-0104 §6
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1742:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:48:    // Prompt fingerprint — populated when IntelligenceProvider was invoked. Shape per ADR-0106.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1743:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:52:    pub children: Vec<Provenance>,
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1744:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:58:    pub warnings: Vec<ProvenanceWarning>,
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1745:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:61:pub enum ProvenanceWarning {
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1746:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:70:`provenance_schema_version` is the schema version of this ADR's envelope structure. A consumer seeing a higher version must parse forward-compatibly — unknown fields are ignored; known fields retain their meaning. The initial version is `1`. Any breaking change requires a new version and a migration path.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1747:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:72:`ability_schema_version` is the ability's I/O schema version per [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §8 — a different concept, retained here for completeness so a consumer reading provenance knows exactly which ability contract produced the output.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1748:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:84:    pub glean_connected: bool,                       // Per ADR-0100
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1749:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:97:3. **Eval reproducibility under fixtures.** In `Evaluate` mode, the fixture's state is deterministic; the snapshot plus the fixture reconstructs the run. [ADR-0110](0110-evaluation-harness-for-abilities.md) (forthcoming — renumbered from 0107) specifies how.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1750:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:99:**Reproducibility is a scoped claim, not an unqualified one.** Full content-level replay of non-fixture runs is not promised and is out of scope for this ADR.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1751:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:103:Trust is a structured record, not a collapsed nested enum. It encodes the weakest trust encountered, the mixing history, and whether the output is safe to authorize mutation on without a trust signal per [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §10.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1752:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:125:    /// policy, or schema-bounded value per ADR-0102 §10.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1753:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:135:    DirectSource { index: usize },         // Points into Provenance.sources
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1754:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:136:    ComposedChild { index: usize },        // Points into Provenance.children
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1755:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:154:4. `contains_stored_synthesis` is true when any source is a stored field known to have been LLM-synthesized (per [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md), stored fields carry a `synthesized_by` marker so this can be detected at read time).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1756:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:158:**`effective` is computed by the provenance builder, not the author.** The author cannot set it; the registry rejects manually-constructed `Provenance` with mismatched `effective` and `contributions`.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1757:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:162:Source attribution references the authoritative `DataSource` taxonomy in [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md). This ADR specifies the shape; that ADR specifies the enum values and lifecycle behavior.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1758:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:166:    pub data_source: DataSource,                 // Defined by ADR-0107
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1759:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:167:    pub identifiers: Vec<SourceIdentifier>,      // Defined by ADR-0107 (extensible enum)
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1760:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:179:    /// Source is context-only, never feeds numeric scoring. Per ADR-0100, Slack and P2 are Context.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1761:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:193:**`evidence_weight` is a contribution weight, not a reliability score.** It is author-supplied (by the ability's planner or synthesizer) and indicates how much this particular source mattered for this specific output. It is not a stored per-source reliability — those are defined by [ADR-0080](0080-signal-intelligence-architecture.md) and consumed separately. We deliberately do not duplicate ADR-0080's reliability into every provenance envelope.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1762:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:195:**`scoring_class` is derived from the `DataSource` per [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md).** It is informational, so consumers can filter context-only sources from scoring analysis.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1763:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:197:**Glean-sourced attribution for invisible content.** When Glean returns an assessment computed from sources DailyOS cannot locally see (e.g., Zendesk tickets the user's Glean account can read but DailyOS cannot), the ability attributes `data_source: Glean` with a `SourceIdentifier::GleanAssessment { assessment_id, cited_sources: Vec<GleanCitedSource> }`. Lifecycle of these invisible sources is governed by the user's Glean policy, not DailyOS's local lifecycle. Details in [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1764:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:210:    pub explanation: Option<SanitizedExplanation>,  // Sanitization rules in ADR-0108
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1765:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:218:    Constant,                                      // Fixed value, not derived
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1766:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:248:Provenance(A) {
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1767:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:250:  children: [Provenance(B), Provenance(C), ...],
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1768:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:264:6. Cycle guard: the registry rejects ability composition cycles at registration time per [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §11.1, so nested `Provenance` trees are guaranteed acyclic.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1769:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:266:**`SourceRef::Child(child_idx, field_path)` uses a stable `composition_id`.** To avoid the brittleness of positional `child_idx`, the `children` vector is indexed by a stable `CompositionId` per declared `composes` entry in the ability's metadata (per [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §7.1). The `child_idx` is the index into the `composes` list, not the runtime invocation order. A `SourceRef::Child(child_idx, field_path)` with a `child_idx` outside the declared `composes` list is a registration error.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1770:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:268:### 7. Provenance Builder Pattern
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1771:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:277:    let mut prov = ProvenanceBuilder::new(ctx, "prepare_meeting");
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1772:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:293:    prov.prompt_fingerprint(completion.fingerprint);  // Shape per ADR-0106
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1773:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:315:Provenance persists anywhere the ability output is stored. Specifically:
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1774:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:317:1. **Maintenance audit table.** [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §8 `MaintenanceAuditRecord` adds a `provenance: Provenance` field. Source revocation triggers a masking pass: a `Provenance` whose sources reference a revoked `DataSource` is replaced with a `ProvenanceMasked` marker per [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md). **Interaction with [ADR-0094](0094-audit-log-and-enterprise-observability.md):** ADR-0094's append-only JSONL security audit remains unchanged. The `maintenance_audit` SQLite table is a separate operational log for runtime diagnostics. Provenance content in the operational log is subject to masking; the JSONL security log is unchanged.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1775:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:319:2. **Outbox table.** [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §2 outbox entries add a `provenance: Provenance` field. Outbox provenance captures the ability's full output-time provenance, including the invocation that generated the pending external mutation.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1776:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:321:3. **Planned mutations.** [ADR-0104](0104-execution-mode-and-mode-aware-services.md) §3 `PlannedMutation` adds a `provenance_ref: InvocationId` field pointing into the ability's provenance envelope. Plans do not carry a full duplicated provenance; they reference the envelope by invocation ID and field path, preventing storage duplication.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1777:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:323:4. **Source revocation behavior.** Revoking a source invalidates derived artifacts per [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md)'s lifecycle rules, which may be "purge" (destructive) or "flag for re-enrichment" (preservation) depending on the source class. ADR-0105 defines how masking presents to consumers; ADR-0107 defines when purge vs. flag applies.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1778:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:325:**Storage format.** Provenance is stored as JSON in a single column per containing record. Indexes on `invocation_id`, `ability_name`, `produced_at`, and `data_source` (via a normalized xref table) support the queries [ADR-0103](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) §8 requires. A full JSON-column approach is feasible at the six-user scale; if scale changes, a normalized `provenance` / `provenance_sources` split can be introduced without changing the envelope contract.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1779:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:333:**Hard truncation.** When a provenance envelope exceeds 1MB at finalize time, composition subtrees are collapsed from deepest first into a `ProvenanceWarning::DepthElided` summary carrying aggregate source counts and trust classification. Truncation is a finalize-time concern; the full tree never leaves the ability in its raw form above the hard limit.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1780:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:340:2. **Trust boundary is enforceable and closes the laundering hole.** [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §10 rejects mutations authorized by `Untrusted` output at the registry layer, and `contains_stored_synthesis` catches the case where stored AI output is surfaced by a Read ability.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1781:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:343:5. **Source revocation can cascade correctly.** Provenance references `DataSource` via [ADR-0107](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md), and lifecycle behavior (purge vs. flag) is governed by that ADR. Masking shape is governed by [ADR-0108](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1782:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:348:1. **Every ability pays an authoring cost.** Provenance building is part of the ability's job. Contributors must think about source attribution when writing synthesis.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1783:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:349:2. **Provenance can be large.** Deep composition with full field attribution produces substantial JSON. Soft budget warns; hard truncation bounds worst-case.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1784:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:355:1. **Attribution drift.** The mapping from output fields to sources drifts as the ability evolves. Mitigation: [ADR-0110](0110-evaluation-harness-for-abilities.md) (forthcoming — renumbered) cross-checks sample attributions against LLM self-evaluation during eval runs.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1785:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:357:3. **Storage volume growth.** Provenance retained indefinitely alongside outputs accumulates. Mitigation: same retention as output; no separate provenance retention policy.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1786:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:358:4. **`composition_id` drift.** An ability's declared `composes` list changes between versions, invalidating stored `SourceRef::Child` references. Mitigation: registry's version-gating in [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) §8 applies — major version bumps for breaking changes.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1787:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:364:- [ADR-0102: Abilities as the Runtime Contract](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md) — Defines `AbilityOutput<T>` wrapper; §9 Rule 5 requires provenance; §10 consumes `TrustAssessment`; §11.3 requires composition merge.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1788:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:365:- [ADR-0103: Maintenance Ability Safety Constraints](0103-maintenance-ability-safety-constraints.md) — §8 maintenance audit records add a `provenance: Provenance` field per §8 of this ADR.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1789:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:366:- [ADR-0104: ExecutionMode and Mode-Aware Services](0104-execution-mode-and-mode-aware-services.md) — `mode` and clock injection for `produced_at`; `PlannedMutation` adds a `provenance_ref` field.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1790:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:367:- [ADR-0094: Audit Log and Enterprise Observability](0094-audit-log-and-enterprise-observability.md) — Coexistence: ADR-0094's append-only JSONL security audit is unchanged; this ADR's provenance lives in operational `maintenance_audit` SQLite table with masking.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1791:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:368:- [ADR-0102](0102-abilities-as-runtime-contract.md), [ADR-0098](0098-data-governance-source-aware-lifecycle.md) — Trust classification and source lifecycle background.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1792:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:369:- **[ADR-0106: Prompt Fingerprinting and Provider Interface Extension](0106-prompt-fingerprinting-and-provider-interface.md)** — Specifies `PromptFingerprint` shape, canonicalization, and amendments to [ADR-0091](0091-intelligence-provider-abstraction.md).
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1793:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:370:- **[ADR-0107: Source Taxonomy Alignment](0107-source-taxonomy-alignment.md)** — Authoritative `DataSource` enum, `SourceIdentifier` extensibility, and lifecycle behavior per source class.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1794:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:371:- **[ADR-0108: Provenance Rendering and Privacy](0108-provenance-rendering-and-privacy.md)** — Per-surface rendering rules, actor-filtered display, `ProvenanceMasked` shape, sanitization of `explanation` text, and P2 publication safety.
.docs/plans/wave-W3/_prompts/_logs/DOS-301.log:1795:.docs/decisions/0105-provenance-as-first-class-output.md:372:- **ADR-0109 (forthcoming): Temporal Primitives in the Entity Graph** — Defines trajectory types referenced from provenance when an ability consumes trajectory inputs.
