.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-219.log:6653:   142	- ADR-0113 §5 tombstone behavior is now triggered by `WrongSubject` (per-subject tombstone) and `MarkFalse` (broad tombstone), not by an untyped UI gesture.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-219.log:6661:   150	- `corrected_to: None` — "this content does not belong to this entity; I don't know whose it is." Tombstone the claim at the asserted subject only; do not propose a new attachment.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-219.log:6662:   151	- `corrected_to: Some(SubjectRef)` — "this content belongs to that entity instead." Tombstone at the asserted subject; propose (not commit) a new claim at the corrected subject with the same claim_text, full provenance preserved, `actor = 'user_correction'`. The corrected claim enters via the standard propose/commit path so it gets the same gate as any other claim.
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-219.log:6664:   153	The inference method that produced the wrong attachment receives `subject_evidence` downweight `-0.3`. After repeated `WrongSubject` feedback against the same `InferenceMethod` for the same source class, the inference method gets globally suppressed for that source class (threshold: 5 instances within 30 days).
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-219.log:6686:    33	│   │   └── expected_provenance.json # Expected provenance envelope (with field-level attributions)
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-219.log:6714:   112	[prepare_meeting]
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-219.log:6723:   121	Judge models invoke a fixture-replayed provider with a dedicated judge prompt that asks for structured rubric scores. Judge outputs are themselves subject to prompt fingerprinting and stored per run for audit.
