.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-219.log:6862:- `src-tauri/src/abilities/prepare_meeting/` (new directory — split into `build_brief.rs` + `publish.rs` + `maintenance.rs`)
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-219.log:6865:- Bundle-5 fixture seed data (coordinate with W6-A; stub if W6-A hasn't landed)
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-219.log:6890:- "About this" affordance implementation: does each section/bullet in `MeetingBrief` carry an inline `SourceAttribution`, or does the ability return a top-level provenance map keyed by field path?
.docs/plans/wave-W5/_prompts/_logs/DOS-219.log:6900:- W4-B (DOS-216): Transform fixtures use replayed judge completions. The fixture for `prepare_meeting` must include both `provider_replay.json` (LLM reply) and `expected_provenance.json` (field attribution). Stub if needed.
