    12	
    13	## Things to be aware of
    14	
    15	- The release gate command is the **v1.4.0 ship criteria in code**. It must exit zero against bundles 1+5 on the seeded workspace or v1.4.0 does not tag.
    16	- Two invocation modes: **automated** (`cargo run --bin release-gate` or `pnpm release-gate` against seeded bundles, hermetic) and **manual** (developer runs against their real dev workspace and captures evidence artifact — this is the "dogfood" gate).
    17	- "Golden Daily Loop" = the core product loop: entity context populated → meeting brief generated → user corrections accepted → next brief reflects corrections. Bundles 1+5 together exercise this full loop.
    18	- The release gate is a **consumer** of W6-A (bundles), W6-B (bleed detection tests), and W5 pilots (abilities running end-to-end). It aggregates their evidence into one exit code + artifact.
    19	- Evidence artifact format matters — it must be machine-readable (for CI) and human-readable (for the v1.4.0 tag proof bundle). Think JSON with a summary markdown section.
    20	- Depends on: W6-A bundles, W6-B detection, W5 pilots (DOS-218 + DOS-219). All must be merged before this gate can produce a passing run.
