    35	- `.docs/plans/wave-W6/DOS-283-plan.md` — bundle load API the gate uses
    36	- `.docs/plans/wave-W6/DOS-288-plan.md` — bleed detection test names the gate must invoke
    37	- `.docs/plans/wave-W4/DOS-216-plan.md` — harness report format the gate aggregates
    38	- `.docs/plans/v1.4.0-waves.md` §"W6 merge gate" — exact list of what the gate must assert
    39	
    40	## Specific design decisions to record in §3
    41	
    42	- Binary vs shell script: `cargo run --bin release-gate` gives Rust-native DB/test access; a shell script wrapping `cargo test` is simpler but can't load the workspace DB for manual mode. Which is right?
